                        "glosses": [
                            "Spanish fly, Lytta vesicatoria (syn. Cantharis vesicatoria)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d435483a-f667-3806-bf2d-dd132d3761d5",
                        "entry_id": "a94f9783-8f45-3d16-b146-7cc21e113e0c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Spanish fly; a vesicant extracted from the beetle, popularly held to have aphrodisiac properties."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9117cf9d-fbed-45d6-8344-bf5e73cc630e",
                                "sense_id": "d435483a-f667-3806-bf2d-dd132d3761d5",
                                "text": "I can make the most subtle sauces yield up their secret—whether it be white arsenic, rosalgar, mercury sublimate, or cantharides."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7c6f65e9-d9ef-40c6-823a-ff5e3d475789",
                                "sense_id": "d435483a-f667-3806-bf2d-dd132d3761d5",
                                "text": "Madame de Pompadour used tincture of cantharides to regain the love of Louis XV."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e993ffce-4952-4ad0-a8cf-d677f942bae9",
                                "sense_id": "d435483a-f667-3806-bf2d-dd132d3761d5",
                                "text": "Speaking her name, it was as if he spake pure cantharides. ‘Quick,’ she panted. ‘There is time before they are all about. Again.’"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b62433a0-58d1-40dd-a5d2-0035cecba2a7",
                                "sense_id": "d435483a-f667-3806-bf2d-dd132d3761d5",
                                "text": "It’s lucky that Carol had taken the precaution of obtaining some cantharides; without them the evening might have been a dead loss."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f37841bb-e03e-48a9-8cd6-f6d52c26f358",
                                "sense_id": "d435483a-f667-3806-bf2d-dd132d3761d5",
                                "text": "Basically Louis's drug dealer and pimp, Richelieu, known for opium recipes to fit all occasions, is also credited with the introduction into France of the cantharides, or Spanish fly."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
